this shop in istanbul has been a refuge  for mccarran since she and her daughter  left northwest china five years ago  her husband and two other children were  left behind in ching young she hasn't  heard from them since  she fears a u.n report that condemns  china's treatment of uyghurs and other  muslim minorities will largely go  ignored  it's been five years of us living here  china has killed our young people and  left our children orphaned the united  nations isn't doing enough  michelle bachelet released the report 13  minutes before her term as u.n human  rights chief ended it found that uyghurs  and other mostly muslim groups and  detention camps have been subjected to  torture including forced medical  treatment and sexual and gender-based  violence  this is not a case of turks or uighurs  or muslims or jews this is a case of  humanity we're not calling for china to  stop just because we're uyghurs any  person with a heart and brain must know  that this is wrong  china has denied any abuses it says his  policies in qing young fight what it  calls terrorism and provides uighurs  with better economic opportunities  the so-called assessment is orchestrated  and produced by the us and some western  forces and is completely illegal and  void  countless stories of torture and  separation are shared within the uyghur  community  abdusalam says he hasn't heard from his  brother in five years  this report should have come out earlier  this isn't something that can be put on  hold when a group is being destroyed  it's not appropriate for humanity just  to watch for a couple of years  the report recommends the chinese  government take steps to release uyghurs  detained in training centers prisons or  detention facilities the uyghur  community hopes for the same but fears  their cause will largely be ignored at  home  and abroad katya lopez  al jazeera
 

